From: armSeb <armSeb@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: krait-cc: fix the auxiliary source of krait-cc-v2

krait-cc-v2 (MSM8974) registers a shared "acpu_aux" clock (GPLL0/2) for
the secondary muxes, but names their parent "apu_aux": the auxiliary
source is never found and the secondary muxes can only use QSB.

On MSM8974 the secondary mux selects QSB with 0 and the auxiliary clock
with 2 (downstream clock-krait-8974.c), the opposite of the map used for
krait-cc-v1 since commit 8e456411abcb ("clk: qcom: krait-cc: fix wrong
parent order for secondary mux"). Use a map of its own for v2.

Signed-off-by: armSeb <armSeb@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/krait-cc.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/krait-cc.c
index f29d6dd1f..7636e3d86 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/krait-cc.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/krait-cc.c
@@ -29,6 +29,15 @@ static unsigned int sec_mux_map[] = {
 	0,
 };
 
+/*
+ * MSM8974 (krait-cc-v2): QSB is source 0 and the auxiliary clock source 2
+ * (downstream clock-krait-8974.c).
+ */
+static unsigned int sec_mux_map_v2[] = {
+	0,
+	2,
+};
+
 static unsigned int pri_mux_map[] = {
 	1,
 	2,
@@ -166,7 +175,7 @@ krait_add_sec_mux(struct device *dev, int id, const char *s,
 	mux->lpl = id >= 0;
 	mux->mask = 0x3;
 	mux->shift = 2;
-	mux->parent_map = sec_mux_map;
+	mux->parent_map = unique_aux ? sec_mux_map : sec_mux_map_v2;
 	mux->hw.init = &init;
 	mux->safe_sel = 0;
 
@@ -191,7 +200,8 @@ krait_add_sec_mux(struct device *dev, int id, const char *s,
 		sec_mux_list[1].fw_name = parent_name;
 		sec_mux_list[1].name = parent_name;
 	} else {
-		sec_mux_list[1].name = "apu_aux";
+		/* registered by krait_cc_probe() */
+		sec_mux_list[1].name = "acpu_aux";
 	}
 
 	ret = devm_clk_hw_register(dev, &mux->hw);
